USC: a mutex lock deschedules

USP counts LOCK among the instructions which always deschedule, so internal
registers can't be live across one, but IsDeschedAfterInst didn't include
ILOCK and internal register allocation could keep a value in one across the
lock of an atomic.  USP then failed to finalise the program ("Internal
registers live after descheduling instruction"), e.g. for atomics in a loop.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c b/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c
index a971428..1dc18e7 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/inst_usc.c
@@ -17524,6 +17524,8 @@ IMG_BOOL IsDeschedAfterInst(PCINST psInst)
 			#if defined(OUTPUT_USPBIN)
 			psInst->eOpcode == ITEXWRITE ||
 			#endif //defined(OUTPUT_USPBIN)
+			/* USP treats LOCK as always descheduling */
+			psInst->eOpcode == ILOCK ||
 			psInst->eOpcode == IIDF
 	   )
 	{
